Feature: Enterprise Context Framework
  As a CACM article reader in enterprise leadership
  I need AI security guidance relevant to business operations
  So that I can make informed decisions about enterprise AI deployment

  Background:
    Given the target audience includes CTOs, CISOs, and AI governance leaders
    And guidance must integrate with existing enterprise frameworks
    And recommendations must be actionable within 90 days

  @contract @E1
  Scenario: Current enterprise AI practices assessment
    Given typical enterprise AI deployment patterns
    When analyzed for security vulnerabilities
    Then should identify common guardrail tools (LLM Guard, content filters)
    And should assess current risk management frameworks
    And should identify gaps in mathematical validation

  @contract @E2
  Scenario: Regulatory compliance integration
    Given regulatory frameworks for enterprise compliance
    When mathematical constraints are considered
    Then should identify gaps in current compliance frameworks
    And should translate mathematical limits to policy recommendations
    And should provide compliance roadmap for 90-day implementation

  @contract @E3
  Scenario: Enterprise risk framework translation
    Given mathematical impossibility of perfect AI security
    When translated to enterprise risk management
    Then should shift from "risk elimination" to "risk acceptance" framework
    And should provide quantitative risk assessment methods
    And should integrate with existing SOX, SOC2, ISO 27001 frameworks

  @contract @E4
  Scenario: Business impact quantification
    Given real-world AI security incidents with financial data
    When analyzed for enterprise budget implications
    Then should provide cost-benefit analysis of security approaches
    And should quantify ROI of mathematical validation vs security theater
    And should include implementation timeline and resource requirements

  @contract @E5
  Scenario: Balaji credibility and institutional backing
    Given UW-Whitewater NSA-designated cybersecurity center
    When leveraged for enterprise credibility
    Then should establish institutional authority for recommendations
    And should provide third-party validation of mathematical approaches
    And should connect to broader cybersecurity community expertise

  @edge @E6
  Scenario: Enterprise technology stack integration
    Given diverse enterprise technology environments
    When mathematical validation tools are deployed
    Then should integrate with existing security operations centers
    And should work with current threat detection platforms
    And should provide APIs for enterprise security orchestration

  @security @E7
  Scenario: Executive communication framework
    Given need to communicate mathematical limits to board level
    When preparing executive presentations
    Then should provide board-ready risk assessment summaries
    And should translate technical findings to business language
    And should include actionable recommendations for governance committees